<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine peso ends higher on inflows.</title>
<headline>Philippine peso ends higher on inflows.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- Aug 27 -------------------------</p>
<p>* Central Bank raises trading range</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Philippine peso continued to rise, ending on Tuesday at 26.195 pesos from 26.209 on heavy dollar inflows into the stock market, traders said.</p>
<p>In view of the heavy inflows, traders said the Central Bank set the pace for a stronger peso when it raised its desired trading range, quoting a buy at 26.194 and a sell at 26.224 pesos. Its previous bid and offer rates were at 26.20 and 26.24.</p>
</text>
